  <!--
    Individual blog posts (blog-post.html?slug=...) live in Firestore and are
    added/edited from the admin panel, so they can't be listed here as static
    entries — a URL sitemap can't safely include a query-string page per post
    without a build step that reads the database. Two ways to close this gap:

      1. Best long-term fix: give each post its own real path (e.g. a Cloud
         Function or static export that generates /blog/<slug>.html), which
         also helps these pages rank on their own.
      2. Fastest fix with the current setup: a small script (Node, or a
         scheduled Cloud Function) that queries the `blogPosts` collection
         where published == true and regenerates this sitemap.xml with one
         <url> block per post, e.g.:
           https://glyphicpalette.com/blog-post.html?slug=<slug>
         Run it whenever a post is published/unpublished, or on a daily timer.

    Ask me and I can write that generator script.
  -->

